[center][size=6][b]Relics Reforged[/b][/size]
[size=3]Move one effect from a relic you don't need onto one you want to keep.[/size][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]
You finally rolled the effect you wanted... on a relic whose other two effects are useless. Relics Reforged adds a forge to [b]Relic Rites[/b] at the Roundtable Hold: pick an effect on a [b]donor[/b] relic and transfer it onto a [b]target[/b] relic, replacing one of its effects.

[list]
[*][b]Always a legal relic.[/b] The result is always a combination the game itself could have rolled for that relic: every effect must fit one of the relic's slot tables, exclusive effects can't stack, and effects are re-sorted the way the game sorts them. The mod never creates impossible relics; it only cuts down the RNG.
[*][b]It has a cost.[/b] The donor and [b]3 sacrifice relics[/b] are destroyed, and you pay [b]murk[/b].
[*][b]Curses travel with their effect.[/b] Moving a Deep effect that comes with a curse moves the curse too. A cursed effect can replace an uncursed one and vice versa, as long as the game also rolls that relic with that mix of cursed and uncursed effects.
[*][b]Your build is safe.[/b] Favorites, equipped relics and relics used in vessels or presets can't be sacrificed. They can be the donor, so you can keep relics with the effects you want as favorites: the forge warns you where it is in use before confirming, and those slots are left empty.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Rules[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Normal relics forge with normal relics, Deep relics with Deep relics.
[*]Sacrifices: exactly 3. Each one is worth 1, 2 or 3 points (Delicate, Polished, Grand). The target needs at least 3 / 5 / 7 points (1 / 2 / 3 effects).
[*]Murk: 2,000 / 4,000 / 7,000 for a target with 1 / 2 / 3 effects, ×1.5 for Deep relics (3,000 / 6,000 / 10,500).
[*]Forge limit per relic: 1 / 1 / 2 forges (1 / 2 / 3 effects). Forged effects are shown in gold.
[*]Fixed relics (the ones that always come with the same effects) can't be forged.
[*]Only at the Roundtable Hold, with Relic Rites open.
[/list]
These are the defaults: see [b]Settings[/b] to change them.

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]
The first time the game starts with the mod, it creates [b]RelicsReforged\relics_reforged.ini[/b] next to the DLL (updates don't overwrite it). Edit it and restart the game to change the key (F1-F12, Insert, Delete, Home, End, PageUp, PageDown) and controller button (R2 or L2) that open the forge, the number of sacrifices (0-9), the minimum points, the murk cost, the Deep multiplier, the forge limit (0 = no limit), the menu language and how many save backups to keep.

[size=4][b]How to use[/b][/size]
In Relic Rites, with the cursor on your equipped relic slots, press [b]F7[/b] (keyboard) or [b]R2 / RT[/b] (controller), or click "F7: Forge relics" at the bottom.
[list=1]
[*]Choose the relic to improve and the effect to replace.
[*]Choose the donor and the effect to transfer.
[*]Choose 3 sacrifices.
[*]Check the preview (cost, points, forge count) and forge. Forging asks for confirmation twice.
[/list]
The forge looks and sounds like the game's own menus: relic and effect icons, search, the same filter as Relic Rites (color, size, type, favorites and up to 3 effect conditions) and sorting. It works with [b]mouse, keyboard and controller[/b]; while it's open, the game doesn't receive your inputs.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Elden Ring Nightreign 1.3.3.[/b] On any other game version the mod stays off and shows a notice for the first minute; the game runs normally.
[*][url=https://me3.help]me3[/url] 0.13 or newer. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenringnightreign/mods/213]ME3 Manager[/url] is optional.
[*]Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenringnightreign/mods/3]Seamless Co-op[/url], to play with friends.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Relics Reforged is a regular DLL mod: [b]RelicsReforged.dll[/b] and, next to it, the [b]RelicsReforged[/b] folder (the settings file and the log are created there). Install it like any other DLL mod:
[list]
[*][b]ME3 Manager (recommended):[/b] install it from Nexus inside ME3 Manager, or drag the downloaded zip into it, and launch from ME3 Manager. [b]With Seamless Co-op:[/b] keep Seamless in your game folder and add [b]Game\SeamlessCoop\nrsc.dll[/b] as an [b]external mod[/b] with [b]load_early[/b] on (advanced options), as ME3 Manager recommends.
[*][b]Your own me3 profile:[/b] unzip into your mods folder and add the DLL to your .me3. For the profile me3 creates (nightreign-default.me3), unzip into its nightreign-mods folder and replace the line [b]natives = [][/b] with these lines (if you keep natives = [], me3 refuses the profile with "duplicate key"):
[code]savefile = "NR0000_RelicsReforged.sl2"

[[natives]]
path = 'nightreign-mods/RelicsReforged.dll'[/code]
The savefile line keeps the mod off your normal save. With Seamless in the same profile you can leave it out (Seamless uses its own save) and add another [[natives]] block with its nrsc.dll (your own game path) and [b]load_early = true[/b]. In any other .me3, add the [[natives]] block and delete its natives = [] line if it has one.
[*][b]No other mods:[/b] download the optional [b]Standalone[/b] file, unzip it anywhere (not inside the game folder) and double-click [b]RelicsReforged.me3[/b]. It plays offline on a copy of your save.
[/list]
Only players who want to forge need the mod (tested in Seamless Co-op with a player without it). Other DLL loaders (like Elden Mod Loader) should work too, but haven't been tested.

[size=4][b]Saves and safety[/b][/size]
The mod works on whatever save the game loads.
[list]
[*][b]Standalone profile:[/b] a copy of your save (NR0000_RelicsReforged.sl2). Your normal save is never touched.
[*][b]Seamless Co-op:[/b] the Seamless save (NR0000.co2 by default).
[*][b]Your own profile without Seamless:[/b] your normal save, unless you add [b]savefile = "NR0000_RelicsReforged.sl2"[/b] to the .me3, above its first line that starts with [ (recommended: me3 copies your save to it the first time).
[*][b]Automatic backup:[/b] before the first forge of every session, your save is copied to %APPDATA%\RelicsReforged\backups (the last 10 are kept).
[*]me3 keeps the game offline. [b]Do not use this mod online.[/b]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Other mods (More Map Variations and similar)[/b][/size]
Relics Reforged loads alongside other mods in the same me3 profile. The forge uses the relic rules the game loaded, so mods that change relics through their own regulation.bin work: the effects they add to the random pools can be forged too. If a mod comes with its own .me3 file, copy RelicsReforged.dll and the RelicsReforged folder next to it and add these lines at the end of that .me3:
[code][[natives]]
path = 'RelicsReforged.dll'[/code]
Tested offline with More Map Variations and Weapons Mod Merge 2.1.8.3; it hasn't been tested on that mod's own online server.

[size=4][b]Languages[/b][/size]
The forge follows the game's language: Spanish if the game is in Spanish, English otherwise. Relic and effect names always come from the game itself, in your language.

[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Tested at 1920x1080. The menu scales with the screen height; other resolutions and aspect ratios haven't been tested yet.
[*]Controllers: tested with a PlayStation controller through Steam Input. Xbox controllers should work but haven't been tested.
[/list]
Found a bug? Please attach [b]RelicsReforged\relics_reforged.log[/b] (next to the DLL) to your report.

[size=4][b]Keeping your forged relics[/b][/size]
Forged relics are stored in the save like any other relic and don't need the mod to exist.
[list]
[*][b]Unsupported game update:[/b] keep playing the same way. The mod stays off, but the save and your forged relics load as usual.
[*][b]Seamless:[/b] they are in the Seamless save (NR0000.co2); play Seamless without the mod and they are still there.
[*][b]On a save copy[/b] (the standalone profile, or a savefile line in your own profile): they are only in NR0000_RelicsReforged.sl2, which moves on separately from your normal save. To keep them without the mod, close the game, back up NR0000.sl2 and replace it with a copy of NR0000_RelicsReforged.sl2 renamed to NR0000.sl2 (this brings over all the progress of the copy).
[*]Taking a save used with the mod online is at your own risk: the relics are combinations the game can roll, but we can't promise nothing gets flagged.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Remove the mod from ME3 Manager, or delete RelicsReforged.dll and the RelicsReforged folder (and the lines you added to your .me3), or the standalone folder. Delete %APPDATA%\RelicsReforged too if you don't want the forge record and the save backups. If you played on a save copy, read [b]Keeping your forged relics[/b] first.

[size=4][b]Credits[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/garyttierney/me3]me3[/url], the mod loader.
[*][url=https://github.com/veeenu/hudhook]hudhook[/url] and [url=https://github.com/ocornut/imgui]Dear ImGui[/url] ([url=https://github.com/imgui-rs/imgui-rs]imgui-rs[/url]), for the in-game menu.
[*]Smithbox and SoulsFormats, whose param definitions and file formats made the research possible.
[*]All icons, textures, texts and sounds are read from your own game install: nothing from the game is redistributed.
[/list]
Source code (MIT license): [url=https://github.com/IgnacioBianchi-cmd/relics-reforged]github.com/IgnacioBianchi-cmd/relics-reforged[/url]

[line]

[spoiler]
[size=4][b]Español[/b][/size]

[b]Qué hace[/b]
Pasá un efecto de una reliquia que no te sirve a otra que querés conservar. En Ritos de reliquias, en la Mesa Redonda, elegís un efecto de una reliquia [b]donante[/b] y reemplaza uno de la reliquia [b]receptora[/b].
[list]
[*][b]Siempre una reliquia legal:[/b] el resultado es una combinación que el juego podría haber generado para esa reliquia. El mod no crea reliquias imposibles, solo reduce cuánto azar hace falta.
[*][b]Tiene un costo:[/b] la donante y [b]3 sacrificios[/b] se destruyen, y se paga [b]murk[/b].
[*][b]La maldición viaja con su efecto.[/b] Un efecto con maldición puede reemplazar a uno sin ella y al revés, siempre que el juego también genere esa reliquia con esa mezcla de efectos con y sin maldición.
[*][b]Tu build está a salvo:[/b] las favoritas, las equipadas y las que están en recipientes o preajustes no pueden ser sacrificios. Sí pueden ser donantes, así podés guardar como favoritas las reliquias con los efectos que querés: antes de confirmar, la forja avisa dónde está en uso, y esos espacios quedan vacíos.
[/list]

[b]Reglas[/b]
[list]
[*]Normales con normales, de las profundidades con de las profundidades.
[*]3 sacrificios de 1, 2 o 3 puntos (delicada, bruñida, grandiosa). La receptora pide al menos 3 / 5 / 7 puntos (1 / 2 / 3 efectos).
[*]Murk: 2.000 / 4.000 / 7.000 según los efectos de la receptora, ×1,5 si es de las profundidades (3.000 / 6.000 / 10.500).
[*]Límite de forjas por reliquia: 1 / 1 / 2. Los efectos forjados se ven en dorado.
[*]No se forjan las reliquias fijas (las que siempre traen los mismos efectos).
[*]Solo en la Mesa Redonda, con Ritos de reliquias abierto.
[/list]
Son los valores por defecto: todo se puede cambiar en [b]RelicsReforged\relics_reforged.ini[/b], que se crea junto a la DLL la primera vez que arranca el juego (las actualizaciones no lo pisan): tecla y botón para abrir la forja, cantidad de sacrificios (0-9), puntos mínimos, murk, multiplicador de las profundidades, límite de forjas (0 = sin límite), idioma del menú y copias del save.

[b]Cómo se usa[/b]
En Ritos de reliquias, con el cursor en los espacios de reliquias equipadas, apretá [b]F7[/b] (teclado) o [b]R2 / RT[/b] (mando), o hacé clic en "F7: Forjar reliquias". Elegí la reliquia a mejorar y el efecto a reemplazar, la donante y su efecto, y 3 sacrificios; revisá la vista previa y forjá (pide confirmación dos veces). Funciona con mouse, teclado y mando.

[b]Requisitos[/b]
Elden Ring Nightreign 1.3.3 (en otra versión el mod se apaga y avisa), [url=https://me3.help]me3[/url] 0.13 o más nuevo (ME3 Manager es opcional) y, para jugar con amigos, Seamless Co-op.

[b]Instalación[/b]
Es un mod DLL común: [b]RelicsReforged.dll[/b] y, al lado, la carpeta [b]RelicsReforged[/b] (ahí se crean la configuración y el registro). Se instala como cualquier mod DLL:
[list]
[*][b]ME3 Manager (recomendado):[/b] instalalo desde Nexus dentro de ME3 Manager, o arrastrá el zip descargado, y arrancá desde ME3 Manager. [b]Con Seamless Co-op:[/b] dejá Seamless en la carpeta del juego y agregá [b]Game\SeamlessCoop\nrsc.dll[/b] como [b]mod externo[/b] con [b]load_early[/b] activado (opciones avanzadas), como recomienda ME3 Manager.
[*][b]Tu propio perfil de me3:[/b] descomprimí en tu carpeta de mods y agregá la DLL a tu .me3. Para el perfil que crea me3 (nightreign-default.me3), descomprimí en su carpeta nightreign-mods y reemplazá la línea [b]natives = [][/b] por estas (si dejás natives = [], me3 rechaza el perfil con "duplicate key"):
[code]savefile = "NR0000_RelicsReforged.sl2"

[[natives]]
path = 'nightreign-mods/RelicsReforged.dll'[/code]
La línea savefile hace que el mod no trabaje sobre tu save normal. Con Seamless en el mismo perfil podés no ponerla (Seamless usa su propio save) y agregar otro bloque [[natives]] con su nrsc.dll (con la ruta de tu juego) y [b]load_early = true[/b]. En cualquier otro .me3, agregá el bloque [[natives]] y borrá su línea natives = [] si la tiene.
[*][b]Sin otros mods:[/b] descargá el archivo opcional [b]Standalone[/b], descomprimilo donde quieras (no dentro de la carpeta del juego) y hacé doble clic en [b]RelicsReforged.me3[/b]. Juega sin conexión sobre una copia de tu save.
[/list]
Solo necesitan el mod los jugadores que quieran forjar (probado en Seamless Co-op con un jugador sin el mod). Otros loaders de DLLs (como Elden Mod Loader) deberían funcionar, pero no se probaron.

[b]Saves[/b]
El mod trabaja sobre el save que cargue el juego: con el perfil standalone, una copia de tu save (NR0000_RelicsReforged.sl2); con Seamless, el save de Seamless; con tu propio perfil sin Seamless, tu save normal, salvo que agregues [b]savefile = "NR0000_RelicsReforged.sl2"[/b] al .me3, antes de su primera línea que empieza con [ (recomendado). Antes de la primera forja de cada sesión se guarda una copia en %APPDATA%\RelicsReforged\backups. No uses este mod online.
Las reliquias forjadas quedan en el save y no necesitan el mod: si el juego se actualiza y el mod todavía no, seguí jugando igual (el mod se apaga, el save carga igual). Si jugaste sobre una copia, están solo en NR0000_RelicsReforged.sl2: para conservarlas sin el mod, con el juego cerrado respaldá NR0000.sl2 y reemplazalo por una copia de NR0000_RelicsReforged.sl2 renombrada a NR0000.sl2 (pasa todo el progreso de la copia). Llevar online un save usado con el mod corre por tu cuenta.

[b]Otros mods (More Map Variations y parecidos)[/b]
Relics Reforged se carga junto con otros mods en el mismo perfil de me3. La forja usa las reglas de reliquias que cargó el juego, así que funciona con mods que cambian las reliquias con su propio regulation.bin. Si un mod trae su propio .me3, copiá RelicsReforged.dll y la carpeta RelicsReforged junto a él y agregá al final de ese .me3:
[code][[natives]]
path = 'RelicsReforged.dll'[/code]
Probado sin conexión con More Map Variations and Weapons Mod Merge 2.1.8.3; no se probó en el servidor online propio de ese mod.

[b]Idioma[/b]
El menú está en español si el juego está en español; si no, en inglés. Los nombres de reliquias y efectos salen del propio juego.

Si encontrás un error, adjuntá [b]RelicsReforged\relics_reforged.log[/b] (junto a la DLL).

Código fuente (licencia MIT): [url=https://github.com/IgnacioBianchi-cmd/relics-reforged]github.com/IgnacioBianchi-cmd/relics-reforged[/url]
[/spoiler]
